import 'system_ui_language.dart';

class GuideUiCopy {
  const GuideUiCopy._(this._values);
  final Map<String, String> _values;

  String operator [](String key) =>
      _values[key] ?? _copies['English']![key] ?? key;

  static GuideUiCopy forLanguage(String language) =>
      GuideUiCopy._(_copies[language.trim()] ?? _copies['English']!);

  static GuideUiCopy forSystemLocale() => forLanguage(systemUiLanguageName());

  static const Map<String, Map<String, String>> _copies = {
    'English': {
      'confirm': 'Confirm',
      'close': 'Close',
      'lobbyTitle': '[ User Guide ]',
      'modeTitle': 'Talk Mode Guide',
      'circleTitle': 'Circle Talk Guide',
      'scenarioTitle': 'Scenario Talk Guide',
      'studyTitle': 'Study Room Guide',
      'lobbyBody':
          "1. Converse comfortably in your native language\nStealthVox is a space where users can naturally converse with AI in their native language and turn those conversations into study materials.\n\n2. You can freely mix foreign languages.\nYou can speak in your native language, in a foreign language, or in a mixture of your native language and a foreign language. Don't worry about forming perfect sentences; just speak as you normally would.\n\n3. Conversations become learning material\nMaterials created from conversations are organized in the study room and used in a variety of ways as learning materials for relistening, role exchange speaking, shadowing, and tutoring.\n\n4. Practice English and foreign languages as your everyday language\nRather than studying to get the correct answer, try repeating what you actually want to say. If you enjoy the materials without pressure, you can practice English as a daily language.\n\n5. Chat and practice together with Duo Connect\nYou can invite acquaintances or family members to the conversation and talk about your daily life as comfortably as if you were talking on the phone. When the call is over, the conversation remains as English learning material, allowing you to effectively practice the conversation patterns you actually used.\n\nYou can also practice each other's language by calling someone who wants to learn a foreign language. The invited partner can also choose the language they want to speak and the language they want to learn, so both people can learn the language they want separately. During a conversation, you can communicate naturally in different languages, like a universal interpreter.\n\nI hope this will also be helpful to those who want to learn Korean while speaking naturally with Korean acquaintances.",
      'modeBody':
          "Duo Connect · Invitational direct conversation\nThis is a function that allows you to talk naturally in each other's real voices with the person you called through the invitation link, and collect language study materials from the call. After the call ends, the conversation continues into the study room.\n\nDuo Connect · Invitational all-round interpreter\nThis is a global all-purpose interpretation mode that provides real-time interpretation when you speak with your partner in your native language through an invitation link.\n\nCircle Talk · Community conversation\nGet AI recommendations or enter your desired community directly. AI becomes a member of the circle and naturally converses according to the tone, interests, and mood of the field.\n\nScenario Talk · Real-life situation conversation\nYou will receive endless recommendations for creative and specific roles and situations, and practice realistic business and daily conversation.\n\nDialogue session (10 minutes)\nIn Circle Talk and Scenario Talk, conversation history is saved in 10-minute increments. Even after saving, you can continue the story based on recent conversations and a short summary on the same screen. You don't have to spend all 10 minutes — you can talk as much as you want and then leave, and your conversation up to that point will be recorded.\n\nIn Circle Talk and Scenario Talk, even if you are talking for 10 minutes, what you said and the AI's response are saved after you finish, so one conversation is not cut into two.\n\nStarting 30 seconds before the session ends, the top time display counts down the remaining seconds, and starting 10 seconds before the session ends, the dot blinks orange.\n\nThe remaining seconds are displayed in the remaining time slot starting 30 seconds before the session ends, and the billing indicator blinks orange in the last 10 seconds. When saving is complete, the remaining time display returns.\n\nDuring these 30 seconds, the remaining time is deducted as usual.\n\nBilling indicator\nBilling in progress\nBilling stop — automatic stop when microphone is on standby (autopose)",
      'circleBody':
          "This is a mode where you create your own interests, occupations, or communities and talk to AI.\n\nWhen you enter a desired circle, AI becomes a member of that circle and communicates naturally, reflecting the atmosphere, tone of voice, and interests.\n\nexample\n• Indian Export Trading Company\n• Startup Development Team\n• Stock Traders Meeting\n• Hospital staff\n• Car club\n\nAlternatively, you can create your own circle of your choice.\n\nTips for use\n✓ Talk comfortably as if you were talking to a real colleague.\n✓ Feel free to use industry terms or expressions that suit your interests.\n✓ As the conversation continues, the AI ​​reflects the context of the circle and makes the conversation more natural.\n\nStep 1 · Step 2\nStep 1 is the same as the chat room so far. AI speaks the same conversational language as we do. When I enter the room, I always start with Step 1.\n\nIf you press the Step 1 button below during a conversation, Step 2 will begin from the next conversation. The AI ​​speaks in the language you chose in the lobby, and you just have to keep answering in your own language — this is listening training. Pressing it again returns to Step 1 and the conversation flow continues.\n\n✓ In Step 2, if possible, listen and answer without looking at the screen. If you don't understand, just ask again.\n\nDialogue session (10 minutes)\nOne session can be up to 10 minutes long. You don't have to spend all 10 minutes — you can talk as much as you want and then leave, and your conversation up to that point will be recorded. Even after 10 minutes, you won't be interrupted or left the room — your conversation will be saved and you can continue on the same screen. The AI ​​continues the conversation by remembering the essence of the previous conversation until it leaves the room.\n\nEven if you are talking for 10 minutes, what you said and the AI's response are saved after you finish, so one conversation is not cut into two.\n\nStarting 30 seconds before the session ends, the top time display counts down the remaining seconds, and starting 10 seconds before the session ends, the dot blinks orange.\n\nCreate your own circle and experience natural English conversation within it.",
      'scenarioBody':
          "This is a mode where you divide roles and talk to AI, just like in a real situation.\n\nBefore starting, you can check the scenario and AI/user roles or modify them directly.\n\nOnce the scenario is decided, the AI ​​will speak first. Try speaking as naturally as the character shown on screen. AI also maintains its assigned role and communicates.\n\nStep 1 · Step 2\nStep 1 is the same as the chat room so far. AI speaks the same conversational language as we do. When I enter the room, I always start with Step 1.\n\nIf you press the Step 1 button below during a conversation, Step 2 will begin from the next conversation. The AI ​​speaks in the language you chose in the lobby, and you just have to keep answering in your own language — this is listening training. Pressing it again returns to Step 1 and the conversation flow continues.\n\nIn Step 2, if possible, do not look at the screen and answer only with your ears. If you don't understand, just ask again.\n\nDialogue session (10 minutes)\nOne session can be up to 10 minutes long. You don't have to spend all 10 minutes — you can talk as much as you want and then leave, and your conversation up to that point will be recorded. Even after 10 minutes, you won't be interrupted or left the room — your conversation will be saved and you can continue on the same screen. The AI ​​continues the conversation by remembering the essence of the previous conversation until it leaves the room.\n\nEven if you are talking for 10 minutes, what you said and the AI's response are saved after you finish, so one conversation is not cut into two.\n\nStarting 30 seconds before the session ends, the top time display counts down the remaining seconds, and starting 10 seconds before the session ends, the dot blinks orange.",
      'studyBody':
          "In the study room, materials from the chat room are delivered, \nPractice opening your mouth and speaking.\n\n📝 Edit your lines — on the chat room front page\nAfter the conversation, take a look at what I said on the first page,\nCorrect any sentences that sound wrong and leave blank lines that are not intended for study.\nIf you click the pencil icon in the speech bubble, you can edit the sentence on the spot.\n\nThis is the same position when you want to leave out a line.\nThere is no separate delete button, and if you delete all contents in edit and save,\nThat line is missing from the screen and learning materials.\n\n✅ Last modified — just one click\nAfter completing the review, click [Final Edit Complete] to lock the line.\nOnce confirmed, it cannot be modified again.\nAfter touching up all the areas to be repaired, press it.\n\nThe confirmed sentences will become the material for all future learning materials.\nSo, you cannot proceed to the next step, Practice, until it is confirmed.\nIf you press Practice before confirming, a confirmation pop-up will appear.\nIf you click [Final Confirmation] there, you will proceed directly to Practice.\n\n🏋️ Practical Tutoring — AI Coaching\nCreate a new sentence with the same structure and say it yourself.\nReceive corrections and feedback from AI.\nLearn patterns by repeatedly creating similar sentences.\n\n🔄 Practice — Role-exchange conversation practice\nPractice like a real conversation by switching roles with the AI.\n\n✨ Clear & Easy · Natural & Sharp — In-depth training\nSpeaking practice sentences written based on conversation material are presented in easy and direct English.\nClear & Easy and Natural & Sharp, which explain the same idea through context and connection.\nPractice echoing and shadowing by dividing each meaningful unit (chunk).\n\n🔊 Volume — Turn down the sound and shadow\nIf you turn down the volume while speaking along\nOnly the AI voice becomes smaller and my voice is recorded as is.\nMy pronunciation remains clear as it is not drowned out by the AI sound.\nYou can check yourself and practice proactively.\nWhen listening to the recording again, turn up the volume.\n\n💾 Keepers — your archive of expressions\nPress and hold the speech bubble you like in the conversation history (about 0.5 seconds).\nThat sentence is included in Keepers.\n\nYou can view the collected sentences from the 🔖 icon at the top of the study room.\nThere are five things you can do for each sentence.\n  ▶ Listen to the sound 🎓 Practical tutoring 🔀 See other expressions\n  ⬆ Move to top 🗑 Delete\n\nKeepers are copied from conversation records, so they are not intertwined.\nEven if you delete the chat room, the sentences it contains remain.\nDeleting from Keepers will leave your original conversation untouched.\n\n⏸️ Auto Pause — Automatic billing protection\nIf there is no response for more than 60 seconds, it will automatically pause and billing will stop.\nIt resumes automatically when you start speaking again or touch the screen.\nRest assured without worrying about fees even if you are away from your seat.",
    },
    'Korean': {
